        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Does ProForm have Black Friday deals in 2026?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On Amazon on 23 November 2026 none of the ProForm treadmill listings carried a Black Friday or deal label in the data we could see, and every price matched 22 November. But three, the Carbon TLS ($559.30), Carbon TLX ($849) and Carbon Pro 2000 ($1,199), were $100 to $540 below ProForm’s own October prices. ProForm’s own site blocked our check that day.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is a good Black Friday price for a ProForm Carbon TLX?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              $849 or less. That was its Amazon price on 22 and 23 November 2026, about $451 below the $1,299.99 ProForm’s site charged on 13 October. At that price it is $350 cheaper than the Carbon Pro 2000, with the same 12 mph and 12% incline on the listings.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the ProForm Carbon Pro 2000 worth it at Black Friday prices?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              At $1,199 on Amazon on 23 November 2026, if you will pay for iFIT Pro at $39 a month or need its 350 lb rating. It is about $101 below ProForm’s October price. Without the membership, the $849 Carbon TLX has the same speed and incline for $350 less.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is iFIT on a ProForm treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              iFIT Train, for the Carbon TL, TLS and TLX, is $15 a month or $144 a year. iFIT Pro, for models with a built-in touchscreen, is $39 a month or $396 a year. Those are the prices on iFIT’s membership page on 23 November 2026; we saw no Black Friday offer on the membership.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you use a ProForm treadmill without iFIT?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. Every ProForm here works as a plain treadmill: you set speed and incline yourself. The membership adds classes that control the treadmill, SmartAdjust, ActivePulse and fitness-app sync. Our guide to using a NordicTrack without iFIT applies to ProForm’s consoles too.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Will ProForm treadmills be cheaper on Cyber Monday?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We do not know, and neither ProForm nor Amazon had said. Cyber Monday is 30 November 2026. If prices change, compare them with the 23 November Amazon prices on this page, not with a list price.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
